.TH SDL_HintCallback 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_HintCallback \- A callback used to send notifications of hint value changes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef void(SDLCALL *SDL_HintCallback)(void *userdata, const char *name, const char *oldValue, const char *newValue);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is called an initial time during
.BR SDL_AddHintCallback
with the hint\(aqs current value, and then again each time the hint\(aqs value changes\[char46] In the initial call, the current value is in both
.BR oldValue
and
.BR newValue \[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
what was passed as
.BR userdata
to
.BR SDL_AddHintCallback ()\[char46]

.TP
.I name
what was passed as
.BR name
to
.BR SDL_AddHintCallback ()\[char46]

.TP
.I oldValue
the previous hint value\[char46]
.TP
.I newValue
the new value hint is to be set to\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This callback is fired from whatever thread is setting a new hint value\[char46] SDL holds a lock on the hint subsystem when calling this callback\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_AddHintCallback (3)
